c14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-326442" "field" "field-4" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "+"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the function $f(x,y)=-x(y-1)^{2}.$ What are the missing entries in the following sign table of $f(x,y)?$\n\n| $y>1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/ef935d673ddc4fa3b66305717f495914c194be2abff63611f8f6be6763e469ce.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/6f2f29dbb53e8c20d963cc48c89af73b1c806985bc77842cbe28b882305ede32.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-x$ | $(y-1)^{2}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,2)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,2)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,0)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/71aceb11f3056308300e3e5c9587d76a281379964caab83f640a6924ffd94298.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<1$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7411d52c7bd30ff865d94a19d5eafd0f7c62f4ed05a70bb40cc33d87ccff4fc1"} {"question" "q-121322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "| $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |"] ["text" "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |"] ["text" "| $-$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $-$ | $+$ |"] ["text" "| $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $+$ |"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121322" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "| $+$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $+$ | $-$ |"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=(x-1)^{2}(y+1).$  What are the missing entries in the sign table of $f(x,y),$ shown below?\n\n| $y>-1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ |  |  |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121274" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=1$ and $y=-1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/23195f0e8657cfbd219f540d6f4403c6bffe1056849e4da43a11b61f4afba76a.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/fad89577df15122a8f80996cbf4f1b840084f51cd93d97a776f5562d59a4cc99.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $(x-1)^{2}$ | $(y+1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-left | $(-2,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Top-Right | $(4,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-2,-2)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(4,-2)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/ba5f76185cc6d2e25204c10e8e25b0bf28b3686cb1d494f87af8f03c4b2f2b66.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>-1$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<-1$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<1$ | $x>1$ |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14