a91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121275" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/image "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/85074c62b73199b0dd1ad8427339c58dae3e1d4ae1df014d94415aea57f24410.png"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Suppose that $f(x,y)=x(y+1).$ Which of the following shaded areas gives the solution to the inequality $f(x,y)\\ge 0?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=-1.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below. Since we have an \"or equal to\" inequality, we use solid lines to divide the plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/599d3a551a20e68989e5de517711ae4c7c73255fb4a9d716797cf90dbb32a4ea.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/43bb5eac3414291bbd844a3608835a6f7be3e5e0dfcc2ae89426581eccdc87b3.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $x$ | $(y+1)$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,0)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,0)$ | $+$ | $+$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-2)$ | $-$ | $-$ | $+$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-2)$ | $+$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nFinally, on our diagram, we shade in the solutions to $f(x,y)\\ge 0$ using the *last* column of the table above.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/18757d46e86eb0d771841e7f5fe13be9ad464ccaf66b7190e7a2a7f02428a88e.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7411d52c7bd30ff865d94a19d5eafd0f7c62f4ed05a70bb40cc33d87ccff4fc1"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/state.json" "file_sha256" "c3566fde9b24eb1f95424406e0207ebca91dc14d0f2400140e3162e126723c74"} {"question" "q-121090" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/3c327630597027f98e30848875cc46041e6668f3c5a990d80b7fdce90f9cdc57.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/4679417a09b9fffe9d08f879f19dffb356fe509e694caa7280ac1be1e3b2a436.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/90b5ba11e4ad6545e74525fe993af172a5526bb107a2d1183c257549d8fad8be.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037232/assets/d92f4081a2eac0048b571b8eb1d0daa8b5cc793c708fb50830c6f20ec9b9e19f.png"] ["image" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1